    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-338750",
      "knowledge_point_id": "f9ccf6b5-e087-5f7b-88e3-3767efbdcc26",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Involving Cosecant with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation  $5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=8-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =8-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\ 6\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})=(48.590\\,377…)^{∘}≈{48.590}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${48.590}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={48.590}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={48.5904}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={48.5904}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062861/assets/b6754300e279bf09409a49aeca7160a319ee90b5a120fe7ac775f12a8444b8af.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{48.590}^{∘} \\\\  & ={131.410}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{49}^{∘},\\,x≈{131}^{∘}.\n$$",
