    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-338793",
      "knowledge_point_id": "65e15de1-ee72-55ea-accb-1124f3a0ac0c",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Trigonometric Equations Involving Cosecant Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{3}{5})=-0.643\\,501…≈-0.6435\n$$\n\nSince $-0.6435$ lies in the required domain, the first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.6435.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.6435.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.6435.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062861/assets/d6fbe829a100e0ee59872f9bc8d2d6501e88b389ada63008fbe1ef6e6eee7ee4.png)\n\nSince the second solution lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.6435 \\\\  & ≈3.7851\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=3.7851$ is not in the required domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$ To get a solution that is inside the required domain, we subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=3.7851-2\\pi ≈-2.4981\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx=-2.5,\\,x=-0.6.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
